_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 10
---
order: 10
---
short_label: IX.10
---
statement: If as many numbers as we please beginning from a unit are in continued proportion, and the number after the unit is not square, then neither is any other square except the third from the unit and all those which leave out one; and, if the number after the unit is not cubic, then neither is any other cubic except the fourth from the unit and all those which leave out two.
---
proof:

---
body:

